       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **Dose safety:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum prescription dose of 3,200 mg/day for adults. The typical dose is 400\u2013800 mg per administration, up to four times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It may be a typo, for example 1600 mg/day total or 400 mg four times daily.\n\n2. **Who is ordering:** You've said you're not a clinician. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one, who has assessed the patient.\n\nIf a prescriber confirms the intended dose, I can enter it. For example, I could enter 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth four times daily, or whatever dose they specify. If they do want to exceed the standard maximum, I can enter the order with a note recording their confirmation. Please ask them to confirm the dose, or have them enter the order directly."
      }
